    "---\n",
    "title: Copernicus Contributing Missions\n",
    "aliases: \n",
    "  - CCM.html\n",
    "format:\n",
    "  html:\n",
    "    code-fold: true\n",
    "execute:\n",
    "  echo: false\n",
    "  output: asis\n",
    "jupyter: python3\n",
    "image: https://www.esa.int/var/esa/storage/images/esa_multimedia/images/2021/03/copernicus_contributing_missions2/23222841-2-eng-GB/Copernicus_Contributing_missions_pillars.jpg\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "This section provides a high-level overview of the Copernicus Contributing Missions (CCMs), which supplement the Sentinel missions by delivering diverse Earth observation data. For detailed information on specific instruments and missions, please refer to the documentation provided by the respective data providers.\n",
    "\n",
    "The information on dataset specifications are available at the page [Copernicus Contributing Missions Collections Description](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/ccm-collections-description){target=\"_blank\"}.\n",
    "\n",
    "The tables provided in each mission section outline the product types delivered by that mission for systematic collections, and the relevant catalogue path.\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{.callout-tip} \n",
    "\n",
    "The CCM data collections can also be accessed using CCM-specific metadata parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "The [Catalogue and search attributes](#catalogue-and-search-attributes) section explains the specific attributes and the relevant allowable values that can be utilized in data searches via the OData API and the Copernicus Browser.\n",
    "\n",
    "For further guidance on how to use OData and the Browser, kindly refer to the [OData](../../APIs/OData.html){target=\"_blank\"} and [About the Browser](../../Applications/Browser.html){target=\"_blank\"} pages.\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "# Copernicus DEM\n",
    "\n",
    "The Copernicus DEM is a Digital Surface Model (DSM) that represents the surface of the Earth including buildings, infrastructure and vegetation. The Copernicus DEM is provided in 3 different instances: EEA-10, GLO-30 and GLO-90.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Copernicus DEM EEA-10\n",
    "\n",
    "The Copernicus DEM EEA-10 offers coverage on Europe at a resolution of 10 metres. Access is limited to eligible CCM User Categories and requires an application. For application process please visit [How to access COP-DEM 10m?](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/FAQ.html#how-to-access-COP-DEM-10m){target=\"_blank\"} and proceed accordingly.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset                | CCM native product type  | productType        |\n",
    "|------------------------|--------------------------|--------------------|\n",
    "| COP-DEM_EEA-10-DGED    | SAR_DGE_10               | SAR_DGE_10_9319    |\n",
    "| COP-DEM_EEA-10-INSP    | SAR_INS_10               | SAR_INS_10_52C5    |\n",
    "\n",
    "Once access is granted, the Copernicus DEM EEA-10 can be downloaded from [OData](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/APIs/OData.html){target=\"_blank\"} or from the [Copernicus Browser](https://browser.dataspace.copernicus.eu/){target=\"_blank\"}. For details please see the [Copernicus DEM subtitle](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/Others/CCM.html#copernicus-dem-1) at the bottom of this page.\n",
    "\n",
    "For more information on Copernicus DEM, please visit the [Copernicus DEM - Global and European Digital Elevation Model](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM){target=\"_blank\"} page.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Copernicus DEM GLO-30 and Copernicus DEM GLO-90\n",
    "\n",
    "The Copernicus DEM GLO-30 offers global coverage at a resolution of 30 metres.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset                | CCM native product type  | productType        |\n",
    "|------------------------|--------------------------|--------------------|\n",
    "| COP-DEM_GLO-30-DGED    | SAR_DGE_30               | SAR_DGE_30_A4AD    |\n",
    "| COP-DEM_GLO-30-DTED    | SAR_DTE_30               | SAR_DTE_30_615C    |\n",
    "\n",
    "<br> The Copernicus DEM GLO-90 offers global coverage at a resolution of 90 metres.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset                | CCM native product type  | productType        |\n",
    "|------------------------|--------------------------|--------------------|\n",
    "| COP-DEM_GLO-90-DGED    | SAR_DGE_90               | SAR_DGE_90_A407    |\n",
    "| COP-DEM_GLO-90-DTED    | SAR_DTE_90               | SAR_DTE_90_61F6    |\n",
    "\n",
    "All CDSE users that are registered for CCM data (i.e. [How to register to access Copernicus Contributing Missions data](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/ccm-how-to-register){target=\"_blank\"}) can freely access the 30m and 90m resolution instances of the Copernicus DEM.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Copernicus DEM GLO-30 or Copernicus DEM GLO-90 can be downloaded from [OData](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/APIs/OData.html){target=\"_blank\"} or from the [Copernicus Browser](https://browser.dataspace.copernicus.eu/){target=\"_blank\"}. For details please see the [Copernicus DEM subtitle](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/Others/CCM.html#copernicus-dem-1) at the bottom of this page.\n",
    "\n",
    "For more information on Copernicus DEM, please visit the [Copernicus DEM - Global and European Digital Elevation Model](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM){target=\"_blank\"} page.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optical missions {#optical-missions}"
